<p dir="auto"><strong>High Severity</strong></p>

<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">SliceFromResponseItem</code> counts only <code class="notranslate">response_item</code> entries to determine how many to skip, but the <code class="notranslate">startOffset</code> it receives from <code class="notranslate">GetTranscriptPosition</code> (and <code class="notranslate">transcriptOffset</code>/<code class="notranslate">countLines</code>) is a <strong>total line count</strong> including <code class="notranslate">session_meta</code>, <code class="notranslate">event_msg</code>, and <code class="notranslate">turn_context</code> lines. This mismatch means the function always skips more response_items than intended. In a typical Codex transcript with at least one <code class="notranslate">session_meta</code> and several <code class="notranslate">event_msg</code> lines, the inflated offset will exceed the actual response_item count, causing <code class="notranslate">SliceFromResponseItem</code> to return <code class="notranslate">nil</code> and the explain --generate feature to fail for Codex.</p>



