**Low Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
When a parent context has a deadline shorter than `defaultSummaryGenerationTimeout` (30s), `context.WithTimeout` adopts the parent's earlier deadline. If that shorter deadline fires, the error message still reports "timed out after 30s" because it hardcodes `defaultSummaryGenerationTimeout` instead of computing the actual elapsed time or checking which deadline triggered. The test in `generator_config_test.go` exercises exactly this path (10ms parent timeout) but only asserts on the substring "timed out", masking the inaccurate duration.
<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->

<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 23b0a798-772c-4964-b45c-9da193294799 -->

