**Medium Severity**

<!-- DESCRIPTION START -->
When the parent context already has a deadline, `generateCheckpointAISummary` skips creating a `context.WithTimeout` with the 30-second `checkpointSummaryTimeout`. This means if a parent context has a deadline *longer* than 30 seconds (e.g., 5 minutes), `timeoutCtx` stays as the parent context and the intended 30-second safety timeout is never applied. Using `context.WithTimeout(ctx, checkpointSummaryTimeout)` unconditionally would be correct, since `WithTimeout` already picks `min(parent_deadline, now+timeout)`, naturally handling both shorter and longer parent deadlines.
<!-- DESCRIPTION END -->

<!-- BUGBOT_BUG_ID: 8da5876e-7c9e-4ba5-92f4-d4d77a914403 -->

